'''333 Carrer Principal''' is a 45-storey mixed-use luxury tower at 333 Carrer Principal in the [[Districte Financer (Original, Sant Cristòfor)|Districte Financer]] of [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], [[Sant Cristòfor]], [[Balboa]]. Completed in 2007, the building houses the five-star '''Grup Pastel Primier Districte Financer''' hotel, the '''Pastel Residences''' luxury condominiums, and an '''[[HRX]]''' department store. At 185 metres (607 ft) to its roof and 192 metres (630 ft) to its antenna tips, it is one of the tallest mixed-use buildings in the Sant Cristòfor waterfront district.

== Architecture ==

The building is a tall rectangular slab with a strong vertical profile. The exterior is divided into two contrasting sections. One side is clad in pale stone or metal panels with narrow windows and long rows of projecting balconies, giving the residential portion shade and texture suited to the tropical climate. The other side is wrapped in blue-grey glass curtain walling with closely spaced horizontal floor lines, presenting a flatter, more reflective commercial appearance.

Near the top, the tower has a large recessed opening or sky terrace beneath a heavy rectangular crown. This feature gives the roofline a distinctive silhouette and likely contains mechanical equipment, an executive lounge, penthouses, or shared amenities. A gold emblem mounted near the crown identifies the building as a flagship Pastel property.

At the base, the tower expands into a broad, multi-level podium with extensive glazing. The podium contains the hotel lobby, restaurants, conference facilities, retail space, parking, fitness facilities, and pool terraces. The podium steps down toward Carrer Principal and is partly screened by mature palm trees and landscaping.

